<title>SPAIN: Tabacalera to sell 9.66 pct Koipe stake.</title>
<headline>Tabacalera to sell 9.66 pct Koipe stake.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's tobacco group Tabacalera said it would sell its 9.66 percent stake in consumer food group Koipe and study the disinvestment of sugar refiner Ebro in order to concentrate on its core tobacco markets.</p>
<p>Tabacalera has a 4.6 percent stake in Ebro.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, Tabacalera also said it was studying the possibility of participating in the competition for the privatisation of Tabaqueira de Portugal.</p>
<p>Tabacalera said it considered the development of the commercial area as a priority and had named Rafael Ordozgoiti de la Rica as commercial director for sales and marketing.</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom, +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
